<main id="main" class="page-main">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>{{ claims.syncTriggers }} PumpSync is designed to minimize server-side storage of health data and credentials.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="content">
        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Effective date</h2>
          <p>Effective date: June 18, 2026</p>
          <p>Last updated: August 3, 2026</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Who operates PumpSync</h2>
          <p>PumpSync is operated by Eric Slutz, an independent developer.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Data PumpSync handles</h2>
          <p>What PumpSync handles depends on how you use it:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>When you choose PumpSync Hosted: App Store subscription transaction identifiers and entitlement status.</li>
            <li>From the app: a PumpSync installation identifier generated by the app.</li>
            <li>During a sync request: Tandem Source username, password, selected region, pump or device identifiers, Tandem pump events, normalized insulin and carbohydrate samples, and service session tokens.</li>
            <li>To operate the backend: sync attempt metadata, redacted error metadata, and technical telemetry.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
          <p>The app stores Tandem credentials in Keychain using device-only accessibility. Tandem credentials are not synced through iCloud by PumpSync.</p>
          <p>The app stores minimal sync metadata and a rolling duplicate-prevention ledger so repeated syncs do not create duplicate Apple Health samples.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Data sent to PumpSync servers</h2>
          <p>The app sends Tandem credentials to the PumpSync backend only during an active HTTPS sync request. The backend uses those credentials to retrieve Tandem Source data for that request.</p>
          <p>A sync request can start manually, or automatically after initial setup when the app opens or during a daily background update.</p>
          <p>{{ claims.backendNonPersistence }}</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Apple Health</h2>
          <p>PumpSync writes insulin and carbohydrate samples to Apple Health only after the user grants Apple Health permission. Apple Health controls whether other apps can read those samples.</p>
          <p>PumpSync does not read unrelated Apple Health data. {{ claims.healthkitNoAds }}</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Backend storage</h2>
          <p>PumpSync stores App Store subscription entitlement state for hosted users, app installation mappings needed to issue PumpSync service tokens, rate-limit events, sync attempt metadata, idempotency records for non-credential endpoints, and redacted operational audit events.</p>
          <p>PumpSync does not store Tandem credentials or Tandem health payloads in backend durable storage.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Sharing</h2>
          <p>PumpSync does not sell user data. PumpSync does not share HealthKit data, Tandem credentials, Tandem tokens, raw Tandem events, or normalized Tandem samples with advertisers, data brokers, or marketing services.</p>
          <p>PumpSync uses these infrastructure providers: Apple (App Store distribution, subscriptions, and Apple Health), Microsoft Azure (hosted backend infrastructure and telemetry), and GitHub (website hosting, source code, and support workflows). Those providers process data only as needed to provide their services.</p>
          {#- TODO(owner) PRIV-07: add an international-transfer sentence naming the hosted backend's Azure region once confirmed, e.g. "PumpSync Hosted runs in Microsoft Azure data centers in <region>; using PumpSync Hosted from other countries transfers sync request data there." The region is not stated in the public docs, so it was not asserted here. #}
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Retention</h2>
          <p>Tandem credentials remain on the user's device until the user deletes them in the app or deletes the app.</p>
          <p>The backend retains account, billing, rate-limit, sync metadata, and redacted operational records only as long as needed to operate PumpSync, troubleshoot issues, meet legal obligations, and protect the service.</p>
          <p>Operational records are kept until a data-deletion request removes them; there is currently no automatic time-based cleanup.</p>
          <p>Raw Tandem events and normalized Tandem samples are discarded by the backend after the sync response is produced. The app discards raw and normalized Tandem payloads after Apple Health confirms the write.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Deletion and your choices</h2>
          <p>Users may delete Tandem credentials in the app. Users may also request deletion of PumpSync hosted server-side metadata using the <a href="/privacy/data-deletion/">account and data deletion instructions</a>.</p>
          <p>Users may also request a copy or correction of the hosted metadata associated with their installation through the same channel.</p>
          <p>Deleting PumpSync does not automatically delete samples already written to Apple Health. Those records are controlled by Apple Health; see <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/108779" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple Support: view and delete Health data</a>.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>PumpSync is not directed at children under 13. A parent or guardian should operate the PumpSync Hosted subscription or self-hosted backend used for a minor's data and must be authorized on the connected Tandem Source account.</p>
          <p>See the <a href="/age-suitability/">age suitability page</a> for guidance for parents and guardians.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Security</h2>
          <p>PumpSync uses HTTPS for network requests. Tandem credentials are stored on device in Keychain and are sent to the backend only for active sync requests. Backend logs and audit events are designed to redact credential and token fields.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>This website</h2>
          <p>This website sets no cookies and uses no analytics, no tracking, and no JavaScript.</p>
          <p>It is hosted on GitHub Pages, which maintains standard server access logs as described in GitHub's privacy statement.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Medical disclaimer</h2>
          <p>{{ claims.medicalDisclaimer }} Users should verify health data and follow guidance from qualified healthcare professionals.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>This policy may be updated as PumpSync changes. The effective date will be updated when material changes are made, and the last-updated date will be revised for any user-visible change.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>For privacy, deletion, or support requests, use the <a href="/support/">support page</a>.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
